% Powder Keg (ability catalogue; category: enemies' powers used against them)
%
% A goblin warband has sent a powder-mule up the ridge, a keg of blackpowder
% strapped to its back. Jolt it, startle it or snare it and the fuse
% catches: the keg winds up (a heavy blow) and goes off where the mule
% stands when it blows - that area catches fire. Down in the grove stands an
% old ent: wood burns (its weakness), and it is heavy (nothing moves it).
% Nothing in the party makes fire. The keg blows once (silenced after).
%
%   camp --- road --- grove (ent; the sap pool, the hollow)
%              |     :
%            ridge (mule)        ridge : grove is a gap (the ravine)
%
% Sight: along every link. The hollow is a chasm in the grove; the sap pool
% is a puddle. The mule is living and follows a taunt (a carrot).
% Two companions, one skill each from eight. The ways:
%   bring the mule to the ent   hook it (two pulls, along the road), or
%                               taunt it from the grove (it walks)
%   light the fuse              lightningFlash (from next door: the jolt
%                               lands before the flasher does), blinding
%                               Flash (from inside), vortex (aimed at the
%                               sap pool: the mule is snared - rooted)
%   in the window               the keg follows the mule: flash it on the
%                               ridge while a friend in the grove taunts
%                               it - it runs down and blows there
%   the hollow                  turn the ent to mist (not heavy, for a
%                               moment) and knock it in: tidalWave,
%                               shieldBash, vortex on the hollow
% Traps:
%   - hooked straight across the ravine, the mule falls, keg and all;
%   - a soaked mule only seizes up under lightning (living, wet and
%     jolted: stunned), and a stunned mule's fuse never catches - a shield
%     bash does the same;
%   - lit anywhere but the grove, the keg is spent;
%   - a vortex on the hollow drops the mule (and anyone near) in it.
% Whoever stands where the keg blows burns too (harmless to the party):
% the team may answer in the window, or take it.

% === Map ===
region(camp).
region(road).
region(grove).
region(ridge).
connected(camp, road).
connected(road, grove).
connected(road, ridge).
gap(ridge, grove).
lineOfSight(camp, road).
lineOfSight(road, camp).
lineOfSight(road, grove).
lineOfSight(grove, road).
lineOfSight(road, ridge).
lineOfSight(ridge, road).
lineOfSight(ridge, grove).
lineOfSight(grove, ridge).
feature(grove, sap, puddle).
feature(grove, hollow, chasm).

% === Companions ===
role(player, player).
role(mage, companion).
at(player, camp).
at(mage, camp).
mana(player, 4).
mana(mage, 4).

% === Enemies ===
role(ent, enemy).
at(ent, grove).
tag(ent, wooden).
tag(ent, heavy).
immune(ent, taunted).

% The powder-mule: jolted, blinded or snared, its keg winds up and goes
% off where the mule is when it blows; once.
role(mule, enemy).
at(mule, ridge).
tag(mule, living).
immune(mule, burning).
behavior(mule, electrocuted, blast, self).
behavior(mule, blinded, blast, self).
behavior(mule, rooted, blast, self).
heavy(blast).
effect(blast, target, spill(flames)).
effect(blast, self, grant(silenced)).

% === Default kit: one skill each (combos replans the whole matrix) ===
knows(player, hook).
knows(mage, lightningFlash).

% === Recipes (level-local: the keg, turned on the ent) ===

% ?e ends up in ?r: there already, brought one link (a hook, a taunt), or
% two, through the area between.
fetch(?e, ?r) :- if(at(?e, ?r)), do().
fetch(?e, ?r) :- if(not(at(?e, ?r))), do(bringTo(?e, ?r, nobody)).
fetch(?e, ?r) :-
    if(at(?e, ?f), \==(?f, ?r), edge(?f, ?m, walk), edge(?m, ?r, walk), \==(?m, ?r)),
    do(bringTo(?e, ?m, nobody), bringTo(?e, ?r, nobody)).

% Light the fuse: a skill that lands a trigger on it, or a vortex on a
% feature of its area that is no pit for it (the snare).
light(?npc) :- if(neutralized(ent)), do().
light(?npc) :-
    if(not(neutralized(ent)), behavior(?npc, ?t, ?ab, self)), do(inflict(?t, ?npc, nobody)).
light(?npc) :-
    if(not(neutralized(ent)), behavior(?npc, ?t, ?ab, self), at(?npc, ?r), feature(?r, ?f, ?fab),
       not(pitTakes(?npc, ?f)), canAct(?a), knows(?a, ?v), effect(?v, foes, moment(grant(?t)))),
    do(cast(?a, ?v, ?f)).

% The keg on the ent: the mule brought and lit; or lit elsewhere, with a
% companion waiting in the grove to bring it in the window; or the ent,
% turned to mist, knocked into the hollow.
win :- if(at(ent, ?r)), do(fetch(mule, ?r), light(mule), confirmStopped(ent)).
win :-
    if(at(ent, ?r), at(mule, ?m), \==(?m, ?r), canAct(?c), canReachNow(?c, ?r)),
    do(walkTo(?c, ?r), light(mule), confirmStopped(ent)).
win :- if(), do(unset(heavy, ent), knockOn(ent, feature(hollow), nobody), confirmStopped(ent)).

funExpect(single_actor_plans, atMost, 0).

% === Choice: one skill each, from eight (htn_components combos) ===
comboSeat(player, 1).
comboSeat(mage, 1).
comboPool(hook).
comboPool(taunt).
comboPool(lightningFlash).
comboPool(blindingFlash).
comboPool(vortex).
comboPool(turnToMist).
comboPool(tidalWave).
comboPool(shieldBash).
comboMinWins(6).
comboMinMethods(3).

goals(win).
